From f6da7521fa8003deaa0439982a87315c256110b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleg Tolmatcev <oleg.tolmatcev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 22:45:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] libdjvu: fix strict-aliasing violation in UTF-8 decoding

GStringRep::UTF8::getValidUCS4() casts a const char * reference to
an incompatible const unsigned char * reference. UTF8toUCS4()
then updates the pointer through the wrong reference type, violating
C++ aliasing rules.

With GCC 16.2 at -O3 on MSYS2 UCRT64, the optimizer assumes that
source is unchanged. Whitespace in languages.xml is then rejected
during context creation; DjView crashes when it uses the null context.

Use a separate unsigned-char pointer for the decoder, then copy its
advanced value back to source.

Tested on MSYS2 UCRT64 with DjVuLibre 3.5.30 and GCC 16.2:
DjView starts after rebuilding with this change.
---
 libdjvu/GString.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libdjvu/GString.cpp b/libdjvu/GString.cpp
index 488aedd..f34b581 100644
--- a/libdjvu/GString.cpp
+++ b/libdjvu/GString.cpp
@@ -2410,7 +2410,11 @@ GStringRep::getUCS4(uint32_t &w, const int from) const
 uint32_t
 GStringRep::UTF8::getValidUCS4(const char *&source) const
 {
-  return GStringRep::UTF8toUCS4((const unsigned char *&)source,data+size);
+  const unsigned char *cursor =
+    reinterpret_cast<const unsigned char *>(source);
+  const uint32_t value = UTF8toUCS4(cursor, data + size);
+  source = reinterpret_cast<const char *>(cursor);
+  return value;
 }
 
 int
